  "text": "What the text is matters too. The lesson's prose sample runs four and a half characters a token. Its Python, under two and a half. Three records cost eighty-nine tokens as JSON, but thirty-three as CSV, because JSON repeats every key on every record. And every model family has its own tokenizer. GPT-3's counts that same JSON as a hundred and twenty. Anthropic says its newest one makes about thirty percent more tokens of the same text than the last. So a model that's twenty percent cheaper per token, but counts thirty percent more tokens, costs you about four percent more.\n\nOne more trap. A chat resends its whole history on every turn. In the lesson's example, ten turns build a conversation seven thousand tokens long. But you're billed for forty-three thousand five hundred input tokens... over six times its length. And each of those tokens reaches the model as an id, which is just a number. Nothing in nineteen seven seven two says berry is anything like cherry.",
